# grade: Π, rejecting: a finding refutes translatability by Table 7's rows; silence affirms nothing.
# Rule 1: local state read as a pure function.  Every mutable local of a
# judged function is reached through its own name only, at any moment, so
# that the function is a fold of states (Table 7's rows for local state; an
# element's update as the whole array's, Cytron et al. 1991, 3.1.1).  The tool
# refuses a second name for a mutable local's storage, an index of a mutable
# local std::array not shown to lie in range, a write that is not a statement
# of its own, a lambda capturing a mutable local by reference, and swap of an
# array with itself.
tool local-state
